        "original_id": "aba59e63-93eb-578b-8625-92d9c78b12c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Markus Feehily, Bobby Fuller\n- Music Groups: The Bobby Fuller Four, Westlife\n- Albums: Fire\n- Songs: Love's Made a Fool of You, I Fought the Law\n- Roles: singers, songwriters, guitarist, vocalist\n- Topics: solo debut albums\n\nFacts:\n- Bobby Fuller was born on October 22, 1942, and he was an American rock singer, songwriter, and guitarist.\n- Bobby Fuller recorded \"Love's Made a Fool of You\" and a cover of \"I Fought the Law\" with his mid-1960s group The Bobby Fuller Four.\n- Bobby Fuller died on July 18, 1966.\n- Markus Feehily was born on 28 May 1980, and he is an Irish singer and songwriter.\n- Markus Feehily was formerly known as Mark Feehily.\n- Markus Feehily was a vocalist in Westlife.\n- Fire is the debut solo studio album by Markus Feehily.",
